---
title: "American Literature"
code: "ENG-246"
category: "english"
credits: "3"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/ENG-112"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: ENG 112, ENG 113, or departmental approval."
---

Examines American literary traditions and texts from diverse time periods, genres, and authors. Analyzes literary works within their historical, cultural, social, and/or literary contexts. Emphasizes skills of close reading. Develops critical thinking and interpretive skills through discussion, interpretation, and analysis of these texts. Lecture 3 hours per week.
